            "parts": [
              "Completed the next bounded research step and saved it in [Note 16](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/01_heat_density_asymptotics/notes/16_ADAPTIVE_FORCING_AND_DIFFERENTIATED_CLOCK_20261024.md).\n\nThe new results:\n\n- Bound the adaptive regulator’s forcing and current source, retaining the cancellations near zeros.\n- Sharpen its static density-bias allowance from \\(O(\\kappa^{-1})\\) to \\(O(\\kappa^{-2})\\).\n- Control the averaged current and density’s time derivative against a moving clock, with error \\(O(L\\kappa^{-7/6})\\)—eventually smaller than the natural \\(L/\\kappa\\) drift scale.\n\nThese results hold on the existing growing positive-time window. **The derivative comparison must retain the lattice’s phase oscillations**; the smooth mean alone does not yet provide the same uniform estimate.\n\nVerification includes 16 exact polynomial checks, nine exact moment checks, and six floating theta comparisons. The proofs and [self-review](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/01_heat_density_asymptotics/reviews/05_ADAPTIVE_TRANSPORT_SELF_REVIEW_20261024.md) remain same-assistant work; independent review and interval certification are still open.\n\nI updated the progress ledger and saved [the next handoff](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/01_heat_density_asymptotics/notes/17_CONTINUATION_AFTER_ADAPTIVE_TRANSPORT_20261024.md). The next substantive task is to control the actual fluctuation covariance needed to close the evolution equation."
